"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the repeated separator pattern: the separator color is the\n    # dominant color in the rows/columns containing regular grid lines.\n    from collections import Counter\n    freq = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    sep = freq.most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    # Grid-line rows/columns are uniformly separator-colored except for\n    # occasional marker cells.\n    rs = [r for r in range(h)\n          if sum(v == sep for v in grid[r]) >= w - 4]\n    cs = [c for c in range(w)\n          if sum(grid[r][c] == sep for r in range(h)) >= h - 4]\n\n    # Keep regularly spaced line positions and read each region's fill color.\n    def regular(lines):\n        if len(lines) < 2:\n            return lines\n        gaps = [b-a for a,b in zip(lines, lines[1:])]\n        step = Counter(gaps).most_common(1)[0][0]\n        return [x for x in lines if (x-lines[0]) % step == 0]\n\n    rs, cs = regular(rs), regular(cs)\n    out = []\n    for r0, r1 in zip(rs, rs[1:]):\n        row = []\n        for c0, c1 in zip(cs, cs[1:]):\n            vals = [grid[r][c] for r in range(r0+1, r1)\n                    for c in range(c0+1, c1) if grid[r][c] != sep]\n            row.append(Counter(vals).most_common(1)[0][0] if vals else sep)\n        out.append(row)\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[7,7,2,2],[7,7,2,2],[6,6,0,0]]}},{"step":67,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1792549401.371,"t1":1792549416.231,"alias":"task-bb525f03","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT (the grid was not a valid ARC grid). Wrong attempts so far: 1.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-bb525f03\nTest input (19x28):\n5 5 5 5 5 5 5 5 5 7 5 5 5 7 5 5 5 5 5 5 5 2 5 5 5 2 5 5\n0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0\n0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 0